{
  "id": "combinations-formula-oq-01-oq-04",
  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "\\det\\bigl(e(a_i, b_j)\\bigr)_{1 \\le i,j \\le n} = \\sum_{\\substack{(P_1,\\ldots,P_n)\\ \\text{non-intersecting}}} \\mathrm{sgn}(\\sigma) \\prod_{i=1}^n w(P_i)",
    "plain": "The Lindström-Gessel-Viennot (LGV) lemma: given strictly ordered source positions a_1 < ... < a_r and target positions b_1 < ... < b_r, the determinant of the matrix M where M_{ij} = C(m + b_j - a_i, m) equals the number of non-intersecting r-tuples of lattice paths.",
    "whyMatters": [
      "Unifies combinatorial determinant identities",
      "Engine behind Catalan numbers, Schur polynomials, plane partition formulas",
      "Connects algebraic (determinant) and combinatorial (path counting) viewpoints"
    ]
  },
  "knowledge": {
    "insights": [
      "The r×r LGV for lattice paths is fully proved in BallotProblemOQ03OQ02.lean (lgv_lemma_rxr)",
      "Well-formedness condition (max source ≤ min target) is necessary for the theorem",
      "The 1×1 case is trivial: det = C(m+b-a, m)",
      "For m=2 sources=[0,1] targets=[2,3]: det=6, verified by native_decide on determinant",
      "For m=3 sources=[0,1] targets=[3,4]: det=50, verified by native_decide on determinant",
      "niTupleCount is noncomputable (uses Classical.dec) — must derive from det, not native_decide",
      "The file imports BallotProblemOQ03OQ02 and presents LGV from the combinations/determinant angle"
    ],
    "builtItems": [
      "CombinationsFormulaOQ01OQ04.lean: 14 theorems, 0 sorries, 0 axioms",
      "lgvConfig1: 1×1 LGV configuration",
      "lgvConfig2: 2×2 LGV configuration with sources [a,a+1] and targets [b,b+1]",
      "lgv_one_by_one: 1×1 det = C(m+b-a,m)",
      "lgv_2x2_det_ex1: det=6 for m=2,a=0,b=2 via native_decide",
      "lgv_2x2_det_ex2: det=50 for m=3,a=0,b=3 via native_decide",
      "lgv_det_is_natural: det is always a natural number (counts path tuples)"
    ],
